<title>CHINA: Tak Sing Alliance year net up 68.66 pct.</title>
<headline>Tak Sing Alliance year net up 68.66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   60.60     vs 35.94</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    18.0	vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  2.99 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    71.09     vs 42.15</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,036.10  vs 953.46</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tak Sing Alliance Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 19-24</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   November 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Tak Sing Alliance is a garment designer, manufacturer and retailer.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on disposal of a subsidiary during the year.</p>
<p>A proposal will be made to the shareholders of the company for the subdivision of the issued and unissued shares of HK$0.50 each in the capital of the company (existing shares) into new shares of HK$0.10 each in the capital of the company (subdivided shares) on the basis that each existing share be dividend into five subdivided shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 19 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs 12 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
